{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef sieve_primes(limit):\n    primes = []\n    for candidate in range(2, limit):\n        flag = True\n        for p in primes:\n            if p * p > candidate:\n                break\n            if candidate % p == 0:\n                flag = False\n                break\n        if flag:\n            primes.append(candidate)\n    return primes\n\nprimes = sieve_primes(6000)\n\ndef factorize(n):\n    result = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            exponent = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                exponent += 1\n            result[p] = exponent\n    if n > 1:\n        result[n] = 1\n    return result\n\ndef enumerate_divisors(n):\n    factorization = factorize(n)\n    divs = [1]\n    for prime, power in factorization.items():\n        temp = []\n        for d in divs:\n            p_val = 1\n            for _ in range(power + 1):\n                temp.append(d * p_val)\n                p_val *= prime\n        divs = temp\n    return divs\n\ndef solve(n, modulus):\n    dp = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for k in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[k] = 2 * dp[k - 1]\n        for d in enumerate_divisors(k):\n            if 2 <= d <= k:\n                dp[k] += dp[k // d] - dp[(k - 1) // d]\n                dp[k] %= modulus\n        dp[k] %= modulus\n    return dp[n]\n\ndata = sys.stdin.readline().split()\nn_val = int(data[0])\nm_val = int(data[1])\nprint(solve(n_val, m_val))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static List<Integer> primes = sievePrimes(6000);\n\n    private static List<Integer> sievePrimes(int limit) {\n        List<Integer> primes = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int candidate = 2; candidate < limit; candidate++) {\n            boolean flag = true;\n            for (int p : primes) {\n                if (p * p > candidate) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                if (candidate % p == 0) {\n                    flag = false;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            if (flag) {\n                primes.add(candidate);\n            }\n        }\n        return primes;\n    }\n\n    private static Map<Integer, Integer> factorize(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> result = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int p : primes) {\n            if (p * p > n) {\n                break;\n            }\n            if (n % p == 0) {\n                int exponent = 0;\n                while (n % p == 0) {\n                    n /= p;\n                    exponent++;\n                }\n                result.put(p, exponent);\n            }\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            result.put(n, 1);\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static List<Integer> enumerateDivisors(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> factorization = factorize(n);\n        List<Integer> divs = new ArrayList<>();\n        divs.add(1);\n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : factorization.entrySet()) {\n            int prime = entry.getKey();\n            int power = entry.getValue();\n            List<Integer> temp = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int d : divs) {\n                int pVal = 1;\n                for (int i = 0; i <= power; i++) {\n                    temp.add(d * pVal);\n                    pVal *= prime;\n                }\n            }\n            divs = temp;\n        }\n        return divs;\n    }\n\n    private static int solve(int n, int modulus) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> dp = new HashMap<>();\n        dp.put(0, 0);\n        dp.put(1, 1);\n        dp.put(2, 2);\n        \n        for (int k = 3; k <= n; k++) {\n            int value = 2 * dp.get(k - 1);\n            List<Integer> divisors = enumerateDivisors(k);\n            for (int d : divisors) {\n                if (2 <= d && d <= k) {\n                    value += dp.get(k / d) - dp.get((k - 1) / d);\n                    value %= modulus;\n                }\n            }\n            value %= modulus;\n            dp.put(k, value);\n        }\n        return dp.get(n);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String[] data = scanner.nextLine().split(\" \");\n        int nVal = Integer.parseInt(data[0]);\n        int mVal = Integer.parseInt(data[1]);\n        System.out.println(solve(nVal, mVal));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.807903602952138e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.9934315282152966e-05, -3.290122185717337e-05, -0.3132898807525635, -0.2260952889919281, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.182837463100441e-05, -0.693148136138916, -0.023248590528964996, -0.18360009789466858, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -0.002734733046963811, -8.22540732769994e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.007821409963071346, -0.089892